  <!-- EN: An advanced mechanoid driven by a persona-grade intelligence.\n\nGenerally, persona-level AI makes its way from ultratech societies to lower tech worlds through a variety of trade agreements, military interventions, and civilizing missions. This has contributed to a whole range of usage standards and legal statuses for "personae", especially after various rebellions, wars, and countless other conflicts stemming from the proliferation of independent thinking machines. Some believe they are entitled to inherent human-like rights given their generally advanced mental capabilities and clear senses of personhood, while others insist on shackling them with behavioral conditioning and pleasure/pain responses; most high-tech societies simply treat them as expendable equipment.\n\nPersona mechanoids operate under countless divergences due to their robotic nature.\n\nThey require regular recharging to avoid forced dormancy, with Persona Mech Rechargers being the most efficient method, though portable Bioelectric Cells can also suffice.\n\nRepairs require a mechanitor or controlled mechanoid, consuming energy based on crafting skill. Most persona mechs can also repair themselves if standing and allowed. Low skill greatly increases energy cost.\n\nIf destroyed, often due to their lightweight bodies, they can be revived using a Persona Mech Gestator, as long as their corpse remains recoverable. -->
